WEBVTT

00:00:00.602 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.631 --> 00:00:06.670
Today, we are talking about classic body massage, also called Swedish massage:

00:00:06.851 --> 00:00:12.350
long strokes, kneading, circles, and light tapping, to help the client relax.

00:00:12.688 --> 00:00:15.230
A good therapist doesn't just have skilled hands.

00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:18.640
They keep the client safe, protect the client's privacy,

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:20.670
and choose exactly the right pressure.

00:00:21.309 --> 00:00:23.231
First, something to be clear about:

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:27.551
the rules and job titles in massage differ from country to country.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:32.831
In some countries, only qualified people may call themselves massage therapists,

00:00:32.781 --> 00:00:34.511
or give therapeutic massage.

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:38.031
This lesson is about relaxation massage in a spa.

00:00:38.432 --> 00:00:41.271
It is training material, not a professional license,

00:00:41.221 --> 00:00:43.631
and it does not teach how to treat injuries.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.471
Find out the rules where you work.

00:00:46.036 --> 00:00:47.629
Something you might come across:

00:00:47.894 --> 00:00:50.051
a client complains of a sore calf,

00:00:50.001 --> 00:00:53.149
and asks you to squeeze it really hard to ease it.

00:00:53.816 --> 00:00:59.064
The therapist looks carefully, and sees that only one calf is swollen, red,

00:00:59.014 --> 00:01:00.589
and warm to the touch.

00:01:01.178 --> 00:01:03.469
That can be a sign of a blood clot in a vein.

00:01:03.935 --> 00:01:06.749
Do not massage, under any circumstances.

00:01:07.098 --> 00:01:09.469
Advise the client to see a doctor the same day.

00:01:09.724 --> 00:01:15.229
If the client has difficulty breathing, or chest pain, call 112 right away.

00:01:15.838 --> 00:01:17.146
So when do you not treat?

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:21.638
A client with a fever, a cold or the flu, who is exhausted,

00:01:21.588 --> 00:01:23.626
or has been drinking alcohol:

00:01:23.808 --> 00:01:24.426
rebook.

00:01:24.838 --> 00:01:30.426
A skin condition that may be contagious, an infection, an open wound, sunburn:

00:01:30.703 --> 00:01:32.026
don't work on that area.

00:01:32.361 --> 00:01:36.266
A fresh injury, like a sprain, a bruise, or a swelling:

00:01:36.615 --> 00:01:38.346
avoid that area completely.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:39.706
Recent surgery:

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.866
wait until the doctor says it is fine.

00:01:42.046 --> 00:01:44.666
Raised, varicose veins in the legs:

00:01:44.772 --> 00:01:45.866
never press on them.

00:01:46.478 --> 00:01:51.561
With an unstable condition, for example high blood pressure, heart disease,

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:54.513
diabetes with numbness in the hands or feet,

00:01:54.702 --> 00:01:55.794
or cancer treatment:

00:01:56.223 --> 00:01:58.674
advise the client to ask their doctor first.

00:01:59.183 --> 00:02:03.699
A client on blood thinners bruises very easily, so the pressure must be very light,

00:02:03.649 --> 00:02:05.474
and they should ask their doctor.

00:02:05.983 --> 00:02:10.114
A pregnant client needs someone with specific training, and special positioning.

00:02:10.301 --> 00:02:12.434
At this basic level, we don't do it.

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:14.194
And we do not diagnose:

00:02:14.304 --> 00:02:17.714
describe what you see, and advise the client to see a doctor.

00:02:18.349 --> 00:02:21.163
The consultation form also asks about oils.

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:24.399
Many massage oils are made from nuts, like almond,

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:27.003
so ask whether the client has a nut allergy.

00:02:27.423 --> 00:02:30.123
Ask about fragrances and essential oils too.

00:02:30.472 --> 00:02:31.083
And ask:

00:02:31.511 --> 00:02:34.283
is there any area the client does not want massaged?

00:02:34.712 --> 00:02:38.683
The client has the right to say no to any area, and to stop at any time.

00:02:39.274 --> 00:02:41.319
Now, the most important part:

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:43.719
draping, and the client's dignity.

00:02:44.037 --> 00:02:45.719
The client undresses alone;

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.679
you step out, and knock before coming back in.

00:02:49.011 --> 00:02:50.839
The client may keep their underwear on.

00:02:51.028 --> 00:02:53.159
The client lies under a large towel.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.831
You uncover only the area you are working on,

00:02:55.781 --> 00:02:58.119
then cover it again as soon as you are done.

00:02:58.528 --> 00:03:02.839
Tuck the edges of the towel neatly and securely, so the client feels safe.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:05.719
Never expose or touch sensitive areas:

00:03:05.821 --> 00:03:08.679
the chest, the genital area, or the buttocks.

00:03:09.094 --> 00:03:12.359
When the client turns over, hold the towel so they stay covered.

00:03:12.786 --> 00:03:16.759
Before moving to a new area, tell the client in a short sentence, like:

00:03:17.107 --> 00:03:18.359
I will do your legs now.

00:03:18.628 --> 00:03:21.879
The client is never surprised, and always feels respected.

00:03:22.403 --> 00:03:25.013
Classic massage has a few main movements.

00:03:25.273 --> 00:03:28.213
Effleurage, long strokes with the whole palm:

00:03:28.317 --> 00:03:31.813
to begin, to warm the muscles, and to link the movements.

00:03:32.135 --> 00:03:34.053
Kneading, or petrissage:

00:03:34.482 --> 00:03:38.772
gently lifting the muscle between the thumb and the fingers, like kneading dough,

00:03:38.722 --> 00:03:40.133
where the muscle is thick,

00:03:40.225 --> 00:03:42.133
such as the shoulders and the calves.

00:03:42.398 --> 00:03:45.013
Small thumb circles, where the muscle is tight.

00:03:45.439 --> 00:03:47.413
And light tapping, or tapotement:

00:03:47.676 --> 00:03:52.053
quick taps with the side of the hand, or a cupped palm, to finish an area.

00:03:52.672 --> 00:03:53.429
Direction:

00:03:53.853 --> 00:03:57.349
on the arms and legs, long strokes go toward the heart:

00:03:57.534 --> 00:04:01.029
from the ankle up to the knee, from the wrist up to the elbow.

00:04:01.424 --> 00:04:03.349
Never press on the spine itself;

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:05.189
work only on either side.

00:04:05.724 --> 00:04:08.949
Over the lower back, near the kidneys, work gently.

00:04:09.378 --> 00:04:14.229
Avoid the hollow behind the knee, the armpits, the front of the neck, and the groin.

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:18.869
In those places, blood vessels and nerves lie close to the surface.

00:04:19.414 --> 00:04:19.998
Pressure:

00:04:20.317 --> 00:04:24.478
massage should feel pleasant, maybe a little intense, but not painful.

00:04:24.823 --> 00:04:27.198
There is no such thing as it has to hurt to work.

00:04:27.627 --> 00:04:31.678
Ask the client at the start, after a few minutes, and when you change areas.

00:04:32.028 --> 00:04:33.278
Watch for signs:

00:04:33.627 --> 00:04:37.596
the client tensing up, holding their breath, pulling a leg away,

00:04:37.546 --> 00:04:39.678
all mean the pressure is too much.

00:04:40.025 --> 00:04:43.998
The tighter the muscle, the slower you should go, not the harder you press.

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:47.612
Your posture decides how long you can last in this job.

00:04:48.196 --> 00:04:51.292
Adjust the bed to the right height, so you don't have to bend over.

00:04:51.719 --> 00:04:57.109
Stand in a lunge, front foot forward, back foot behind, knees slightly bent,

00:04:57.059 --> 00:04:58.092
back straight.

00:04:58.677 --> 00:05:01.897
The pressure comes from your body weight, pushing from your legs,

00:05:01.847 --> 00:05:04.092
not from straining your shoulders and wrists.

00:05:04.521 --> 00:05:06.572
To reach further, step closer;

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:07.932
don't stretch your body.

00:05:08.662 --> 00:05:09.946
A common sequence:

00:05:10.125 --> 00:05:14.685
the client lies face down, and you work on the back, the shoulders, the neck,

00:05:14.635 --> 00:05:16.266
then the backs of the legs.

00:05:16.508 --> 00:05:20.726
The client turns over, and you work on the fronts of the legs, the arms,

00:05:20.676 --> 00:05:22.346
then the shoulders and neck.

00:05:22.604 --> 00:05:24.504
Every salon has its own sequence,

00:05:24.454 --> 00:05:27.866
and the time ranges from half an hour to an hour and a half,

00:05:27.895 --> 00:05:28.906
depending on the treatment.

00:05:29.077 --> 00:05:33.386
As for hygiene, wash your hands before and after every client.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:37.673
Sheets, towels and face cradle covers are fresh for every client,

00:05:37.623 --> 00:05:39.946
and the bed is wiped and disinfected.

00:05:40.142 --> 00:05:43.069
Watch the hand hygiene lesson, the lesson on tools,

00:05:43.019 --> 00:05:45.946
and the lesson on when not to treat a client again.

00:05:46.525 --> 00:05:49.946
When the session is over, invite the client to sit up slowly,

00:05:49.896 --> 00:05:54.202
because getting up fast after lying down for a long time can make them dizzy.

00:05:54.612 --> 00:05:55.882
Offer a glass of water.

00:05:56.461 --> 00:05:59.562
But do not tell the client that massage detoxes the body.

00:05:59.897 --> 00:06:00.602
Be honest:

00:06:00.871 --> 00:06:03.402
massage helps them relax, and feel good.

00:06:03.991 --> 00:06:07.402
After firm pressure, they may feel slightly sore the next day.

00:06:07.751 --> 00:06:09.482
You can keep this in VaraaAi:

00:06:09.827 --> 00:06:13.592
in the internal notes on the client record, write the pressure they like,

00:06:13.542 --> 00:06:14.762
and the areas to avoid.

00:06:15.111 --> 00:06:18.042
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:19.082
See you next time.
